)WSID COURSE
GO←'GO'
LAST←0
STOP←'STOP'
∇DESCRIBE
'COURSE -- APL, LESSON BY LESSON, WITH QUIZZES.'
''
'   START       BEGIN AT LESSON 1.'
'   CONTENTS    THE LESSONS, BY NUMBER AND TITLE.'
'   LESSON N    READ LESSON N; LESSON N S STARTS AT SECTION S.'
'   NEXT        THE LESSON AFTER THE LAST ONE YOU READ.'
'   QUIZ N      QUESTIONS ON LESSON N, MARKED AS YOU GO.'
'   EXAMPLES    THE FUNCTIONS LESSONS 11 TO 14 BRING WITH THEM.'
''
'A LESSON PAUSES BETWEEN SECTIONS SO YOU CAN TRY WHAT IT'
'SHOWS: AT A PAUSE, TYPE AN EXPRESSION OR A SYSTEM COMMAND,'
'GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE A LESSON OR A QUIZ.'
∇
∇CONTENTS
'THE LESSONS. LESSON N READS ONE; QUIZ N ASKS ABOUT IT.'
''
'   1  WHERE YOU ARE'
'   2  NUMBERS'
'   3  VECTORS'
'   4  COMPARISON AND LOGIC'
'   5  REDUCTION AND SCAN'
'   6  SELECTION'
'   7  MATRICES'
'   8  PRODUCTS'
'   9  ORDER AND COUNTING'
'  10  CHARACTERS'
'  11  DEFINING FUNCTIONS'
'  12  BRANCHING'
'  13  INPUT AND OUTPUT'
'  14  ERRORS'
'  15  WORKSPACES'
'  16  THE TWO MODES'
∇
∇START
LESSON 1
∇
∇NEXT
→(LAST≥16)/END
LESSON LAST+1
→0
END:'THAT WAS THE LAST LESSON. CONTENTS LISTS THEM ALL.'
∇
∇LESSON ∆N;∆F
⍝ LESSON N, OR LESSON N S TO START AT SECTION S. LAST IS GLOBAL ON
⍝ PURPOSE: NEXT READS IT, AND )SAVE KEEPS IT. THE LOCALS OF
⍝ EVERYTHING ON THE WAY TO A PAUSE ARE DELTA NAMES, SO THAT WHAT
⍝ THE READER TYPES THERE SEES THEIR OWN NAMES.
∆F←1
→(1=⍴,∆N)/ONE
∆F←(,∆N)[2]
∆N←(,∆N)[1]
ONE:→((∆N<1)∨∆N>16)/BAD
LAST←∆N
→(∆N>14)/NOTYET
→(L1,L2,L3,L4,L5,L6,L7,L8,L9,L10,L11,L12,L13,L14)[∆N]
L1:∆L1 ∆F
→0
L2:∆L2 ∆F
→0
