∇∆L7 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 7: MATRICES'
''
'RESHAPE WITH TWO NUMBERS ON THE LEFT MAKES A MATRIX: ROWS'
'BY COLUMNS, FILLED ROW BY ROW. TRY:'
''
'      M←3 4⍴⍳12'
'      M'
'      ⍴M'
'      ⍴⍴M'
''
'⍴M IS 3 4, BOTH DIMENSIONS. ⍴⍴M IS 2, THE NUMBER OF'
'DIMENSIONS, CALLED THE RANK: A NUMBER HAS RANK 0, A VECTOR'
'1, A MATRIX 2, AND APL GOES ON UPWARDS.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'INDEXING A MATRIX TAKES TWO SUBSCRIPTS, ROW THEN COLUMN,'
'WITH A SEMICOLON BETWEEN. LEAVE ONE OUT TO TAKE ALL OF IT.'
'TRY:'
''
'      M[2;3]'
'      M[2;]'
'      M[;3]'
'      M[1 3;2 4]'
''
'THE LAST PICKS ROWS 1 AND 3 AND COLUMNS 2 AND 4, AND IS A'
'MATRIX OF ITS OWN.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'⍉M IS THE TRANSPOSE, ROWS FOR COLUMNS. A REDUCTION ON A'
'MATRIX RUNS ALONG THE LAST DIMENSION, THE ROWS, AND THE'
'BARRED FORM ⌿ RUNS DOWN THE COLUMNS. TRY:'
''
'      ⍉M'
'      +/M'
'      +⌿M'
'      +/[1]M'
''
'THE BRACKETED NUMBER NAMES THE AXIS: +/[1]M IS +⌿M.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'THE SCALAR FUNCTIONS WORK ON A MATRIX AS ON A VECTOR,'
'ELEMENT BY ELEMENT, AND THE COMMA RAVELS IT BACK INTO A'
'VECTOR. TRY:'
''
'      M×2'
'      M>6'
'      ,M'
'      2 3⍴''ABCDEF'''
''
'A MATRIX PRINTS WITH ITS COLUMNS LINED UP, NUMBERS TO THE'
'RIGHT AND CHARACTERS TO THE LEFT.'
''
'END OF LESSON 7. TYPE QUIZ 7 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q7;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
'WHAT IS ⍴2 3⍴⍳6?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 3 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS (2 3⍴⍳6)[2;1]?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+4 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS +/2 3⍴⍳6?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+6 15 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS +⌿2 3⍴⍳6?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+5 7 9 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS ⍴⍉2 3⍴⍳6?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+3 2 ∆CHECK ∆A
'YOU GOT ';∆S;' OF 5.'
∇
∇∆L8 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 8: PRODUCTS'
''
'THE OUTER PRODUCT, ∘.F, APPLIES F TO EVERY PAIR: EACH'
'ELEMENT ON THE LEFT AGAINST EACH ON THE RIGHT, MAKING A'
'TABLE. TRY:'
''
'      1 2 3∘.×1 2 3'
'      (⍳3)∘.+⍳3'
'      (⍳5)∘.×⍳5'
''
'THE LAST IS THE MULTIPLICATION TABLE, IN ONE EXPRESSION.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'WITH A COMPARISON THE OUTER PRODUCT MAKES A TABLE OF 1S AND'
'0S, WHICH IS OFTEN A SHAPE YOU WANT. TRY:'
''
'      (⍳3)∘.=⍳3'
'      (⍳4)∘.≥⍳4'
''
'THE FIRST IS THE IDENTITY MATRIX; THE SECOND A TRIANGLE.'
'LESSON 9 COUNTS WITH ONE.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'THE INNER PRODUCT F.G COMBINES TWO FUNCTIONS: G BETWEEN'
'THE PAIRS, THEN F REDUCING. +.× IS THE SUM OF PRODUCTS, AND'
'ON MATRICES IT IS THE MATRIX PRODUCT. TRY:'
''
'      1 2 3+.×4 5 6'
'      (2 3⍴⍳6)+.×3 2⍴⍳6'
''
'THE FIRST IS 4+10+18, WHICH IS 32. THE SECOND IS 2 BY 2:'
'EACH ROW OF THE LEFT AGAINST EACH COLUMN OF THE RIGHT.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'ANY TWO FUNCTIONS WILL DO. ∧.= ASKS WHETHER TWO VECTORS'
'AGREE THROUGHOUT, AND +.= COUNTS WHERE THEY AGREE. TRY:'
''
'      ''ABC''∧.=''ABC'''
'      ''ABC''∧.=''ABD'''
'      1 2 3+.=1 5 3'
''
'END OF LESSON 8. TYPE QUIZ 8 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q8;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
'WHAT IS 1 2 3+.×4 5 6?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+32 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS ⍴(⍳2)∘.+⍳3?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 3 ∆CHECK ∆A
'IN (⍳3)∘.×⍳3, WHAT IS THE ELEMENT IN ROW 2, COLUMN 3?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+6 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS ''AB''∧.=''AB''?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+1 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS 1 2+.=1 3?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+1 ∆CHECK ∆A
'YOU GOT ';∆S;' OF 5.'
∇
∇∆L9 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 9: ORDER AND COUNTING'
''
'⍋V IS GRADE UP: NOT THE SORTED VECTOR, BUT THE POSITIONS'
'THAT WOULD SORT IT. INDEXING BY IT DOES THE SORTING. TRY:'
''
'      ⍋3 1 2'
'      V←31 4 15 9'
'      V[⍋V]'
'      V[⍒V]'
''
'⍒ IS GRADE DOWN. THE GRADE IS MORE USEFUL THAN A SORT: IT'
'CAN ORDER A SECOND VECTOR THE SAME WAY, NAMES BY SCORES.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'?N IS A NUMBER FROM 1 TO N, DIFFERENT EACH TIME, AND M?N IS'
'M DIFFERENT ONES: A ROLL, AND A DEAL. TRY:'
''
'      ?6'
'      ?6 6'
'      5?10'
''
'THE SEQUENCE STARTS FROM THE SAME PLACE IN EVERY CLEAR'
'WORKSPACE, SO A PROGRAM USING ? CAN BE RUN AGAIN EXACTLY.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'⊤ AND ⊥ ARE ENCODE AND DECODE, BETWEEN A NUMBER AND ITS'
'DIGITS IN ANY BASE, OR MIXED BASES. TRY:'
''
'      2 2 2 2⊤13'
'      2⊥1 1 0 1'
'      10⊥1 9 8 4'
'      24 60 60⊤3661'
''
'THE LAST TURNS SECONDS INTO HOURS, MINUTES AND SECONDS.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'TO COUNT HOW OFTEN EACH VALUE OCCURS, COMPARE THE VALUES'
'AGAINST THE DATA WITH AN OUTER PRODUCT AND SUM THE ROWS.'
'A TABLE OF 1S AND 0S INDEXED INTO TWO CHARACTERS IS A'
'PICTURE. TRY:'
''
'      C←+/(⍳3)∘.=1 3 2 3 3 1'
'      C'
'      '' *''[1+C∘.≥⍳3]'
''
'END OF LESSON 9. TYPE QUIZ 9 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q9;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
'WHAT IS ⍋3 1 2?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 3 1 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS 5 2 8 SORTED INTO ASCENDING ORDER?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 5 8 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS 2⊥1 0 1?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+5 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS 2 2 2⊤6?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+1 1 0 ∆CHECK ∆A
'HOW OFTEN DO 1 AND 2 EACH OCCUR IN 1 2 2 1 2? TWO NUMBERS.'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 3 ∆CHECK ∆A
'YOU GOT ';∆S;' OF 5.'
∇
∇∆L10 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 10: CHARACTERS'
''
'CHARACTERS GO IN QUOTES, AND A ROW OF THEM IS A VECTOR LIKE'
'ANY OTHER. A QUOTE INSIDE IS DOUBLED. TRY:'
''
'      ''HELLO'''
'      ⍴''HELLO'''
'      ''IT''''S'''
'      ''ABC'',''DEF'''
''
'''A'' IS A SINGLE CHARACTER, A SCALAR, AND ⍴''A'' IS EMPTY AS'
'⍴7 WAS; ,''A'' IS A VECTOR OF ONE.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'COMPARISON, MEMBERSHIP, INDEX-OF, COMPRESSION AND REVERSAL'
'ALL WORK ON CHARACTERS. TRY:'
''
'      ''HELLO''=''L'''
'      ''HELLO''⍳''L'''
'      ''HELLO''∊''AEIOU'''
'      (~''HELLO''∊''AEIOU'')/''HELLO'''
'      ⌽''HELLO'''
''
'THE FOURTH KEEPS THE CONSONANTS: THE VOWELS ARE FOUND BY'
'MEMBERSHIP, NEGATED, AND USED TO COMPRESS.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'A MATRIX OF CHARACTERS IS A LIST OF WORDS, ONE TO A ROW,'
'PADDED WITH BLANKS TO THE LONGEST. TRY:'
''
'      NAMES←3 4⍴''ANN BOB CARL'''
'      NAMES'
'      NAMES[2;]'
'      2 5⍴''HELLOWORLD'''
''
'NAMES[2;] IS THE SECOND WORD, BLANK AND ALL.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'CHARACTERS AND NUMBERS CANNOT BE JOINED WITH A COMMA: THAT'
'IS A DOMAIN ERROR. TO PRINT THEM ON ONE LINE, SEPARATE THEM'
'WITH SEMICOLONS. TRY:'
''
'      ''TOTAL: '';+/1 2 3'
'      ''X IS '';5;'' AND Y IS '';6'
''
'THIS IS MIXED OUTPUT, AND IT IS HOW THIS COURSE PRINTS YOUR'
'SCORE.'
''
'END OF LESSON 10. TYPE QUIZ 10 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q10;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
'HOW MANY CHARACTERS ARE IN ''APL''? TYPE THE NUMBER.'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+3 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS ''BANANA''⍳''N''?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+3 ∆CHECK ∆A
'HOW MANY TIMES DOES A OCCUR IN ''BANANA''?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+3 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS ⌽''APL''? TYPE IT IN QUOTES.'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+'LPA' ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS ''ABC''∊''CAT''?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+1 0 1 ∆CHECK ∆A
'YOU GOT ';∆S;' OF 5.'
∇
∇EXAMPLES
'THE EXAMPLE FUNCTIONS OF LESSONS 11 TO 14, IN THIS WORKSPACE:'
''
'   SQUARE X        X TIMES X                        (11)'
'   A HYP B         THE HYPOTENUSE                   (11)'
'   HELLO           NO ARGUMENT, NO RESULT           (11)'
'   MEAN V          THE AVERAGE, WITH A LOCAL        (11)'
'   COUNT N         1 TO N, ONE A LINE, BY A BRANCH  (12)'
'   FACT N          FACTORIAL, BY RECURSION          (12)'
'   SUMLOOP V       THE SUM, THE LONG WAY            (12)'
'   ASK             READS A VALUE WITH QUAD          (13)'
'   GREET           READS A NAME WITH QUOTE-QUAD     (13)'
'   GUESS           A GUESSING GAME                  (13)'
'   OOPS            FAILS ON ITS SECOND LINE         (14)'
''
'CUBE IS YOURS TO DEFINE, IN LESSON 11. DISPLAY ANY OF THESE'
'AT THE PROMPT WITH ∇NAME[⎕]∇.'
∇
∇R←SQUARE X
R←X×X
∇
∇R←A HYP B
R←((A*2)+B*2)*0.5
∇
∇HELLO
'HELLO.'
∇
∇R←MEAN V;N
N←⍴V
R←(+/V)÷N
∇
∇COUNT N;I
I←1
L:I
I←I+1
→(I≤N)/L
∇
∇R←FACT N
R←1
→(N≤1)/0
R←N×FACT N-1
∇
∇R←SUMLOOP V;I
R←0
I←1
L:→(I>⍴V)/0
R←R+V[I]
I←I+1
→L
∇
∇R←ASK
'HOW MANY?'
R←⎕
∇
∇GREET;W
⍞←'YOUR NAME? '
W←⍞
'HELLO, ',W
∇
∇GUESS;N;G
N←?10
L:'A NUMBER FROM 1 TO 10?'
G←⎕
→(G=N)/WIN
'NO. AGAIN.'
→L
WIN:'YES.'
∇
∇OOPS
'BEFORE'
1 2+1 2 3
'AFTER'
∇
∇∆L11 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 11: DEFINING FUNCTIONS'
''
'A FUNCTION IS DEFINED BETWEEN TWO DELS. THE FIRST LINE IS'
'THE HEADER: THE RESULT, THE NAME, THE ARGUMENT. THE EDITOR'
'NUMBERS THE LINES; A DEL ALONE CLOSES. THIS IS CUBE:'
''
'      ∇R←CUBE X'
'[1]   R←X×X×X'
'[2]   ∇'
'      CUBE 3'
'27'
''
'A DEFINITION IS TYPED AT THE PROMPT, NOT AT A PAUSE. TYPE'
'STOP, DEFINE CUBE, TRY CUBE 3 AND CUBE 1 2 3, THEN TYPE'
'LESSON 11 2 TO COME BACK TO THE NEXT SECTION.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'A HEADER HAS ONE OF SIX SHAPES: WITH OR WITHOUT A RESULT,'
'AND WITH NO ARGUMENT, ONE ON THE RIGHT, OR ONE ON EACH'
'SIDE. THESE ARE IN THE WORKSPACE FOR YOU TO TRY:'
''
'      ∇R←SQUARE X        ONE ARGUMENT'
'      ∇R←A HYP B         TWO: THE HYPOTENUSE'
'      ∇HELLO             NONE, AND NO RESULT'
''
'      SQUARE 7'
'      3 HYP 4'
'      HELLO'
''
'A FUNCTION WITH NO RESULT PRINTS OR CHANGES SOMETHING; IT'
'CANNOT BE USED INSIDE AN EXPRESSION.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'A NAME AFTER A SEMICOLON IN THE HEADER IS LOCAL: IT EXISTS'
'WHILE THE FUNCTION RUNS AND IS GONE AFTER. MEAN USES ONE:'
''
'      ∇R←MEAN V;N'
'[1]   N←⍴V'
'[2]   R←(+/V)÷N'
'[3]   ∇'
''
'      MEAN 2 4 6'
'      N'
''
'N IS A VALUE ERROR AFTERWARDS: THE LOCAL N NEVER TOUCHED'
'ANY N OF YOURS. WITHOUT THE SEMICOLON IT WOULD HAVE.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'TO SEE A FUNCTION, OPEN IT WITH A QUAD IN BRACKETS AND'
'CLOSE IT AGAIN; TO CHANGE A LINE, OPEN IT AT THAT LINE AND'
'TYPE THE NEW ONE. AT THE PROMPT, AFTER THIS LESSON:'
''
'      ∇MEAN[⎕]∇'
'      ∇MEAN[2]R←(+/V)÷⍴V'
'      ∇'
''
')FNS LISTS THE FUNCTIONS IN THE WORKSPACE, AND )ERASE NAME'
'REMOVES ONE. EXAMPLES LISTS THE ONES THIS COURSE BROUGHT.'
''
'END OF LESSON 11. TYPE QUIZ 11 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q11;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
'GIVEN R←X×X IN SQUARE, WHAT IS SQUARE 1 2 3?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+1 4 9 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS 5 HYP 12?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+13 ∆CHECK ∆A
'IN THE HEADER R←MEAN V;N, WHICH NAME IS LOCAL? IN QUOTES.'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+'N' ∆CHECK ∆A
'HOW MANY ARGUMENTS HAS A FUNCTION WITH HEADER R←A F B?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS MEAN 2 4 9?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+5 ∆CHECK ∆A
'YOU GOT ';∆S;' OF 5.'
∇
∇∆L12 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 12: BRANCHING'
''
'LINES OF A FUNCTION RUN IN ORDER UNLESS A LINE SAYS'
'OTHERWISE. → FOLLOWED BY A LINE NUMBER GOES THERE; →0'
'LEAVES THE FUNCTION. A NAME AND A COLON AT THE START OF A'
'LINE IS A LABEL, A NAME FOR ITS NUMBER. COUNT USES ONE:'
''
'      ∇COUNT N;I'
'[1]   I←1'
'[2]   L:I'
'[3]   I←I+1'
'[4]   →(I≤N)/L'
'[5]   ∇'
''
'      COUNT 3'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'LINE 4 IS THE CONDITIONAL BRANCH. I≤N IS 1 OR 0; 1/L IS L'
'AND 0/L IS AN EMPTY VECTOR; AND A BRANCH TO AN EMPTY VECTOR'
'GOES NOWHERE, SO THE NEXT LINE RUNS. THAT IS THE WHOLE OF'
'IF AND WHILE IN THIS APL. FACT USES IT TO STOP RECURSING:'
''
'      ∇R←FACT N'
'[1]   R←1'
'[2]   →(N≤1)/0'
'[3]   R←N×FACT N-1'
'[4]   ∇'
''
'      FACT 5'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'A LOOP IS SELDOM NEEDED. SUMLOOP ADDS A VECTOR THE LONG'
'WAY:'
''
'      ∇R←SUMLOOP V;I'
'[1]   R←0'
'[2]   I←1'
'[3]   L:→(I>⍴V)/0'
'[4]   R←R+V[I]'
'[5]   I←I+1'
'[6]   →L'
'[7]   ∇'
''
'      SUMLOOP 1 2 3 4'
'      +/1 2 3 4'
''
'THE REDUCTION IS SHORTER, FASTER, AND HAS NO BOUNDS TO GET'
'WRONG. REACH FOR A LOOP ONLY WHEN EACH STEP DEPENDS ON THE'
'LAST, AS FACT DOES.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'A BRANCH CAN CHOOSE AMONG SEVERAL LINES: →(A,B,C)[N] GOES'
'TO THE NTH LABEL, AND →((X<0),(X=0),X>0)/NEG,ZERO,POS TO'
'THE FIRST WHOSE TEST IS 1. LESSON IS WRITTEN THAT WAY, AND'
'∇LESSON[⎕]∇ AT THE PROMPT SHOWS IT.'
''
'END OF LESSON 12. TYPE QUIZ 12 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q12;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
'WHAT DOES COUNT 2 PRINT? TYPE THE TWO NUMBERS.'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+1 2 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS FACT 4?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+24 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT LINE NUMBER DOES →0 BRANCH TO?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+0 ∆CHECK ∆A
'WHAT IS SUMLOOP 5 5 5?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+15 ∆CHECK ∆A
'HOW MANY TIMES DOES FACT CALL ITSELF FOR FACT 3?'
∆A←∆READ
→('STOP' ∆IS ∆A)/0
∆S←∆S+2 ∆CHECK ∆A
'YOU GOT ';∆S;' OF 5.'
∇
∇∆L13 ∆F;∆Q
→(S1,S2,S3,S4)[1⌈4⌊∆F]
S1:'LESSON 13: INPUT AND OUTPUT'
''
'A QUAD ON THE RIGHT OF AN ARROW READS A LINE, EVALUATES IT,'
'AND GIVES THE VALUE. ASK DOES THAT:'
''
'      ∇R←ASK'
'[1]   ''HOW MANY?'''
'[2]   R←⎕'
'[3]   ∇'
''
'      ASK'
'      2×ASK'
''
'THE REPLY MAY BE ANY EXPRESSION, 2+3 AS WELL AS 5. THIS'
'PAUSE IS A QUAD TOO, SO ASK ASKS INSIDE IT, AND ANSWERS.'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S2:'A QUOTE-QUAD READS THE LINE AS CHARACTERS, UNEVALUATED. ON'
'THE LEFT OF AN ARROW IT PRINTS WITHOUT ENDING THE LINE, SO'
'A PROMPT AND ITS ANSWER SHARE ONE. GREET USES BOTH:'
''
'      ∇GREET;W'
'[1]   ⍞←''YOUR NAME? '''
'[2]   W←⍞'
'[3]   ''HELLO, '',W'
'[4]   ∇'
''
'      GREET'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S3:'A LINE THAT IS A VALUE PRINTS IT. TO PRINT IN THE MIDDLE OF'
'AN EXPRESSION, ASSIGN TO QUAD: ⎕←2+2 PRINTS 4 AND IS 4. AN'
'EMPTY VECTOR PRINTS AN EMPTY LINE, WHICH IS HOW A BLANK LINE'
'IS MADE. TRY:'
''
'      3×⎕←2+2'
'      '''''
'      ''SUM: '';+/⍳10'
∆TRY
∆Q←∆PAUSE
→∆Q/0
S4:'GUESS PUTS IT TOGETHER: A QUESTION, A QUAD, A COMPARISON,'
'AND A BRANCH BACK UNTIL THE ANSWER IS RIGHT.'
''
'      ∇GUESS;N;G'
'[1]   N←?10'
'[2]   L:''A NUMBER FROM 1 TO 10?'''
'[3]   G←⎕'
'[4]   →(G=N)/WIN'
'[5]   ''NO. AGAIN.'''
'[6]   →L'
'[7]   WIN:''YES.'''
'[8]   ∇'
''
'      GUESS'
''
'THE QUIZZES OF THIS COURSE ARE THE SAME SHAPE, WITH A CHECK'
'OF THE VALUE AND THE SHAPE OF THE ANSWER.'
''
'END OF LESSON 13. TYPE QUIZ 13 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.'
∇
∇∆Q13;∆S;∆A
∆S←0
